    {
      "id": "claim_e7155a2db30d4f658204f4639291bb01",
      "statement": "The sre-tools stage installs ocm, ocm-backplane, osdctl and yq via github_dl exact-asset checksum verification, oc via a GPG-signed OpenShift checksum manifest, and the AWS CLI via a detached publisher signature, each re-validated offline (--network=none --validate-installed) before verify_sre_tools.py combine merges the six per-tool records into /opt/tool-versions.json. Claude Code, OpenCode, the Codex CLI and the pi coding agent each have their own tools-base-derived builder stage that fetches one pinned release through github_dl against a published SHA256 checksum file or exact asset; search-builder adds fd (hard-coded SHA256 constants, no upstream checksum asset) and ripgrep (checksum file) the same way, and tmux-builder independently builds tmux from a SHA256-checked source tarball. The final stage's last network-isolated RUN re-verifies the shipped filesystem offline as sre — architecture, pinned versions/signers for the six SRE tools, and version probes for the four coding agents and two search tools — before the image is tagged.",
