    {
      "id": "claim_85879380fa8944fd9af8d21fb3f7b5f2",
      "statement": "entrypoint.sh unifies the normal-exit and signal-shutdown paths into a single cleanup() function (trapped on EXIT and on SIGTERM/SIGINT/SIGHUP): it immediately re-arms TERM/INT/HUP to a no-op and disarms the EXIT trap to prevent re-entry, sends SIGTERM to CHILD_PID and to the skill-reconciler helper via stop_skill_reconciler, waits up to roughly three seconds for both to actually exit (await_writers), and then runs sync_to_s3 under an outer timeout bounded by SHUTDOWN_SECONDS=105 (with a KILL_GRACE_SECONDS=2 forced kill), sized so METADATA_SECONDS=3 metadata lookups and a MAX_SYNC_SECONDS=85 aws s3 sync fit inside the ECS task's configured stop timeout; the resulting S3 object and its report.json are always marked status unverified because other tasks or ECS Exec sessions can keep writing throughout the window.",
